            0.458
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Solution :",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " One shirt is drawn at random from the carton of 100 shirts. Therefore, there are 100 equally likely outcomes."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.118,
            0.474,
            0.887,
            0.54
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) The number of outcomes favourable (i.e., acceptable) to Jimmy = 88 (Why?) Therefore, P (shirt is acceptable to "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm{Jimmy})=\\frac{88}{100}=0.88"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.546,
            0.833,
            0.613
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) The number of outcomes favourable to "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm{S\\bar{q}\\bar{q}th\\bar{a}=88+8=96\\quad(Why?)}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " So, P (shirt is acceptable to "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm{Sujatha}) = \\frac{96}{100} = 0.96"
            }
          ]
        },
